{"name":"Black Bay","hex":"#474a4e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Black Bay is the debut studio album by British post-rock band Silver Moth, released on Bella Union on April 21, 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6e/Silver_Moth_-_Black_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Bay","wikidata":"Q119709343"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg/500px-DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg/1280px-DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg/500px-DirkvdM_baracoa_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","a